{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":56328,"duration_api_ms":56328,"result":"{\n  \"feature\": \"status-page\",\n  \"summary\": \"Add a public page at /status and a JSON endpoint at GET /api/status. Both show whether the API is available, the backend version and the current environment. One server-side helper, lib/status.ts, produces the data for both, so there is no backend service or new infrastructure. The page is a server component that calls the helper directly instead of fetching its own API over HTTP. The planning reports overlapped in places, so ownership is split as follows. Backend (codex) owns the response type, the helper, the route and the helper's unit tests. Frontend (antigravity) owns the page, its presentational components and their component tests. QA (cursor) owns the endpoint contract tests, the proxy regression test, the documentation, the review and the final verification. Infrastructure (claude) owns the rules for where environment and version come from, and a read-only check of the Vercel settings. No new dependencies, no new environment variables by default, no deploys and no commits by workers. The codex report was empty because it never received the feature text, so backend tasks come from the other reports and still need codex to acknowledge them. The decisions listed under open questions are proposed defaults and must be approved before implementation starts.\",\n  \"architecture\": {\n    \"overview\": \"The helper lib/status.ts is the only source of status data. app/api/status/route.ts wraps it as JSON for monitors and other clients. app/status/page.tsx renders it through the presentational component components/status/StatusView.tsx. Both the route and the page must render at request time so environment and version are never frozen at build time.\",\n    \"data_flow\": [\n      \"The helper exports getStatus(deps?), which resolves the environment, the version and the commit, then checks API availability.\",\n      \"API availability: when NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL is missing or still equals 'https://<project-ref>.supabase.co' (the same rule as lib/data.ts and lib/supabase/proxy.ts), the mode is 'mock'. No network call is made and the result is available=true, status 'ok'. When Supabase is configured, an injectable probe calls a cheap Supabase health endpoint with a 3000 ms timeout and no caching. A successful probe under 1000 ms gives 'ok'. A successful probe at 1000 ms or more gives 'degraded'. An error or a timeout gives 'down'.\",\n      \"GET /api/status returns application/json with Cache-Control: no-store. It returns HTTP 200 for 'ok' and 'degraded', and HTTP 503 for 'down'. It is forced to run at request time using whatever mechanism Next 16 provides; the implementer must check node_modules/next/dist/docs.\",\n      \"The /status page is a server component that awaits getStatus() at request time and passes the result to StatusView. A small client RefreshButton calls router.refresh(). There is no automatic polling.\",\n      \"Environment and version rules, owned by infrastructure: environment uses VERCEL_ENV ('production', 'preview' or 'development') when it is set. Otherwise it uses NODE_ENV, normalized to 'production', 'development' or 'test'. Anything else is 'unknown'. version is the version field of package.json (currently 0.1.0), imported on the server. commit is the first 7 characters of VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA, or null when that variable is not set.\"\n    ],\n    \"files_in_scope\": [\n      \"types/index.ts (add the StatusResponse types; this resolves the frontend report's proposed types/status.ts in favor of the repository's existing convention)\",\n      \"lib/status.ts (new)\",\n      \"app/api/status/route.ts (new, the repository's first Route Handler)\",\n      \"app/status/page.tsx (new)\",\n      \"components/status/StatusView.tsx and components/status/RefreshButton.tsx (new)\",\n      \"components/layout/Footer.tsx (one link, only if approved)\",\n      \"tests/status-lib.test.ts, tests/status-view.test.tsx, tests/status-endpoint.test.ts, tests/status-proxy.test.ts (new)\",\n      \"README.md and docs/engineering/PROJECT_GUIDE.md (documentation)\"\n    ],\n    \"out_of_scope\": [\n      \"The nested resuelvelo/ directory. Only paths at the repository root are in scope.\",\n      \"Changes to proxy.ts, lib/supabase/proxy.ts, vitest.config.ts, next.config.ts or supabase/schema.sql\",\n      \"New npm dependencies, new environment variables, Dockerfiles, CI workflows, deploys, migrations, commits, branches\",\n      \"A new document under docs/. Documentation stays in README.md and PROJECT_GUIDE.md, so MASTER_INDEX.md does not change.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"assignments\": [\n    {\n      \"agent\": \"claude\",\n      \"tasks\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"INFRA-1\",\n          \"description\": \"Freeze contract C-ENV: the rules for resolving environment, version and commit, as described in the architecture section. Confirm that no new APP_ENV or APP_VERSION variable is needed and that .env.example stays unchanged. Deliver the rules to the orchestrator for the contract freeze; do not change repository files.\",\n          \"depends_on\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"INFRA-2\",\n          \"description\": \"Read-only: confirm that the Vercel project exposes VERCEL_ENV and VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA to the runtime in Production and Preview, and that deployment is Vercel's git integration with no custom CI. Report the findings without changing any settings.\",\n          \"depends_on\": [\n            \"INFRA-1\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"scope\": \"No repository files. Read-only inspection of .env.example and the Vercel project settings. Changing .env.example is allowed only if a human approves a new variable.\",\n      \"depends_on\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"agent\": \"codex\",\n      \"tasks\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"BE-1\",\n          \"description\": \"Add StatusLevel, ApiMode, AppEnvironment and StatusResponse to types/index.ts, exactly as written in contract C-TYPES.\",\n          \"depends_on\": [\n            \"INFRA-1\",\n            \"QA-1\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"BE-2\",\n          \"description\": \"Implement lib/status.ts, exporting resolveEnvironment(env), resolveVersion(), resolveCommit(env), isSupabaseConfigured(env) and getStatus(deps?). deps accepts an injectable probe and a clock. Use the mock-mode rule above, a 3000 ms timeout and a 1000 ms degraded threshold. The module must have no network side effects at import time and must never include Supabase URLs, keys or error details in its output.\",\n          \"depends_on\": [\n            \"BE-1\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"BE-3\",\n          \"description\": \"Implement app/api/status/route.ts as a GET handler that calls getStatus(). Return HTTP 200 for 'ok' or 'degraded' and HTTP 503 for 'down', with Cache-Control: no-store and a JSON body. Force request-time execution using the mechanism documented in node_modules/next/dist/docs.\",\n          \"depends_on\": [\n            \"BE-2\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"BE-4\",\n          \"description\": \"Write unit tests for lib/status.ts in tests/status-lib.test.ts. Cover: VERCEL_ENV taking precedence; NODE_ENV fallback; 'unknown' for missing or unsupported values; version equal to package.json; commit shortened or null; mock mode making no probe call; a probe that succeeds fast ('ok'), succeeds slowly ('degraded'), errors ('down') or times out ('down', using fake timers); and a body that contains no secrets. Use vi.stubEnv, vi.unstubAllEnvs, vi.resetModules and dynamic imports.\",\n          \"depends_on\": [\n            \"BE-2\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"scope\": \"types/index.ts (additions only), lib/status.ts, app/api/status/route.ts, tests/status-lib.test.ts. May run npm run test and npm run lint. Must not run typecheck or build, because the single .next/ directory is reserved for QA.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"INFRA-1\",\n        \"QA-1\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"agent\": \"antigravity\",\n      \"tasks\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"FE-1\",\n          \"description\": \"Build components/status/StatusView.tsx, a presentational component following contract C-VIEW. It shows a text label for each state ('ok', 'degraded', 'down') plus a mock-mode note, an indicator that does not rely on color alone (an icon or text with role=status or an aria-label), the version, the commit when present, the environment and the formatted check time. Also build components/status/RefreshButton.tsx, a client component that calls router.refresh().\",\n          \"depends_on\": [\n            \"BE-1\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"FE-2\",\n          \"description\": \"Build app/status/page.tsx, a server component rendered at request time that awaits getStatus() from lib/status.ts and renders StatusView. It must not fetch /api/status over HTTP, must not import Supabase directly, and needs page metadata. Follow the Next 16 conventions in node_modules/next/dist/docs.\",\n          \"depends_on\": [\n            \"FE-1\",\n            \"BE-2\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"FE-3\",\n          \"description\": \"Add one link to /status in components/layout/Footer.tsx. Do this only if a human approves the link; otherwise skip the task and report it as skipped.\",\n          \"depends_on\": [\n            \"FE-2\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"FE-4\",\n          \"description\": \"Write component tests in tests/status-view.test.tsx using @testing-library/react with StatusResponse fixtures. Cover the 'ok', 'degraded' and 'down' states and mock mode. Check the label, version, commit or its absence, the environment, the accessible indicator, and that the refresh button renders.\",\n          \"depends_on\": [\n            \"FE-1\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"scope\": \"app/status/page.tsx, components/status/*, tests/status-view.test.tsx, and components/layout/Footer.tsx only if FE-3 is approved. May run npm run test and npm run lint. Must not run typecheck, build or the dev server, which are reserved for QA. No changes to backend files.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"BE-1\",\n        \"BE-2\",\n        \"QA-1\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"agent\": \"cursor\",\n      \"tasks\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"QA-1\",\n          \"description\": \"Freeze the acceptance criteria and the contracts C-TYPES, C-HTTP, C-HELPER, C-SEC, C-ROUTING, C-VIEW and C-TEST, using the approved answers to the open questions. Get sign-off from the codex and antigravity owners before implementation starts. No code changes.\",\n          \"depends_on\": [\n            \"INFRA-1\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"QA-2\",\n          \"description\": \"Write contract tests for GET in tests/status-endpoint.test.ts, with a '// @vitest-environment node' pragma if needed. In mock mode, check: HTTP 200; content-type application/json; Cache-Control no-store; exactly the agreed keys; valid enum values; and a timestamp in ISO 8601 close to the current time. With a mocked probe failure, check HTTP 503 and status 'down'. Also check that the body contains no Supabase URL, no key and no names or values of environment variables.\",\n          \"depends_on\": [\n            \"BE-3\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"QA-3\",\n          \"description\": \"Write a regression test in tests/status-proxy.test.ts with a mocked createServerClient. Anonymous requests to /status and /api/status must not be redirected by updateSession, while /admin, /proveedor and /mis-cotizaciones keep their redirects.\",\n          \"depends_on\": [\n            \"QA-1\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"QA-4\",\n          \"description\": \"Documentation. In README.md, describe /status and /api/status with an example response and explain the meaning of the HTTP status codes. In the Architecture section of docs/engineering/PROJECT_GUIDE.md, add one line placing lib/status.ts and the route. Run npm run docs:check.\",\n          \"depends_on\": [\n            \"BE-3\",\n            \"FE-2\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"QA-5\",\n          \"description\": \"Review the backend and frontend changes against the frozen acceptance criteria. Check for: no secrets exposed; no Supabase calls from components; no new dependencies; only root paths changed; output that is not cached and rendered at request time; and non-public environment variables read on the server only.\",\n          \"depends_on\": [\n            \"BE-4\",\n            \"FE-4\",\n            \"QA-2\",\n            \"QA-3\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"QA-6\",\n          \"description\": \"Run npm run verify once, in full and on its own, on the integration branch checkout. Confirm in the build output that /api/status and /status are dynamic, not prerendered. A skipped or failed check counts as a failure.\",\n          \"depends_on\": [\n            \"QA-4\",\n            \"QA-5\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"QA-7\",\n          \"description\": \"Browser pass of /status in mock mode on the port 3000 dev server, run after QA-6 so the two do not share .next/. Check the states shown, the refresh button and the Footer link if FE-3 was done. Record that environment and commit on Preview and Production remain unverified until a deploy is authorized; after an authorized deploy, check them using the INFRA-2 findings.\",\n          \"depends_on\": [\n            \"QA-6\",\n            \"INFRA-2\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"scope\": \"tests/status-endpoint.test.ts, tests/status-proxy.test.ts, README.md, docs/engineering/PROJECT_GUIDE.md. Read-only review of every other file in scope. Only QA uses .next/ (typecheck, build, dev server), one process at a time.\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"INFRA-1\",\n        \"BE-3\",\n        \"BE-4\",\n        \"FE-2\",\n        \"FE-4\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"contracts\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"C-ENV\",\n      \"description\": \"environment = VERCEL_ENV when it is one of 'production', 'preview' or 'development'. Otherwise it is NODE_ENV normalized to 'production', 'development' or 'test'. Anything else is 'unknown'. version = the version field of package.json, imported on the server; process.env.npm_package_version must not be used. commit = the first 7 characters of VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA, or null. No new environment variables.\",\n      \"owner\": \"claude\",\n      \"consumers\": [\n        \"codex\",\n        \"cursor\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"C-TYPES\",\n      \"description\": \"In types/index.ts: type StatusLevel = 'ok' | 'degraded' | 'down'; type ApiMode = 'supabase' | 'mock'; type AppEnvironment = 'production' | 'preview' | 'development' | 'test' | 'unknown'; interface StatusResponse { status: StatusLevel; api: { available: boolean; mode: ApiMode; latencyMs: number | null }; version: string; commit: string | null; environment: AppEnvironment; timestamp: string }. timestamp is in ISO 8601. No other fields are allowed.\",\n      \"owner\": \"codex\",\n      \"consumers\": [\n        \"antigravity\",\n        \"cursor\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"C-HELPER\",\n      \"description\": \"lib/status.ts exports getStatus(deps?: { probe?: (signal: AbortSignal) => Promise<void>; now?: () => Date }): Promise<StatusResponse>, plus resolveEnvironment, resolveVersion, resolveCommit and isSupabaseConfigured. Mock mode never calls the probe. The timeout is 3000 ms and a successful probe at 1000 ms or more is 'degraded'. Errors map to 'down' without exposing any detail. Importing the module has no side effects.\",\n      \"owner\": \"codex\",\n      \"consumers\": [\n        \"antigravity\",\n        \"cursor\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"C-HTTP\",\n      \"description\": \"GET /api/status returns a StatusResponse as JSON with Content-Type application/json and Cache-Control: no-store. It returns HTTP 200 for 'ok' or 'degraded', mock mode included, and HTTP 503 for 'down'. It runs at request time and is never prerendered. Only GET is supported.\",\n      \"owner\": \"codex\",\n      \"consumers\": [\n        \"cursor\",\n        \"external uptime monitors\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"C-SEC\",\n      \"description\": \"Responses and the page show only the fields in C-TYPES. No Supabase URL or key, no dump of process.env, no stack traces and no raw error messages. Non-public environment variables are read on the server only.\",\n      \"owner\": \"codex\",\n      \"consumers\": [\n        \"antigravity\",\n        \"cursor\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"C-ROUTING\",\n      \"description\": \"/status and /api/status stay public and are not added to rutaProtegida in lib/supabase/proxy.ts. proxy.ts and lib/supabase/proxy.ts do not change.\",\n      \"owner\": \"codex\",\n      \"consumers\": [\n        \"antigravity\",\n        \"cursor\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"C-VIEW\",\n      \"description\": \"StatusView takes props { data: StatusResponse } and renders without fetching anything. Each state has a text label, the indicator does not rely on color alone, mock mode shows a note, and the commit is hidden when it is null. RefreshButton is a client component that calls router.refresh().\",\n      \"owner\": \"antigravity\",\n      \"consumers\": [\n        \"cursor\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"C-TEST\",\n      \"description\": \"Test files live under tests/ and match *.test.ts(x). Environment stubs use vi.stubEnv, vi.unstubAllEnvs and vi.resetModules with dynamic imports. Tests make no real network calls. Route tests may use a per-file '// @vitest-environment node' pragma; the global config does not change. Workers may run test and lint; only QA runs typecheck, build, verify or the dev server.\",\n      \"owner\": \"cursor\",\n      \"consumers\": [\n        \"codex\",\n        \"antigravity\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"integration_order\": [\n    \"1. Contract freeze, with no code: INFRA-1, then QA-1 with sign-off from codex and antigravity. A human approves the open questions. INFRA-2 can run in parallel at any point before QA-7.\",\n    \"2. Merge the backend onto feature/status-page/integration in order: BE-1, BE-2, BE-3, BE-4. Test and lint must pass for the backend files.\",\n    \"3. Merge the frontend onto the integration branch: FE-1, FE-2, FE-4, then FE-3 if it was approved. Test and lint must pass.\",\n    \"4. Merge the QA tests and documentation: QA-3 (can be written once QA-1 is done and merged at this point), QA-2, QA-4.\",\n    \"5. Review (QA-5), then one full npm run verify with no other process running (QA-6).\",\n    \"6. Browser pass in mock mode (QA-7). Checking Preview and Production stays pending until a human authorizes a deploy.\"\n  ],\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"GET /api/status returns JSON matching C-TYPES exactly, with no extra keys, and the header Cache-Control: no-store.\",\n    \"In mock mode (NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL missing or set to the placeholder), the endpoint returns HTTP 200, status 'ok', api.mode 'mock' and api.available true, and makes no network call.\",\n    \"When the Supabase probe errors or exceeds 3000 ms, the endpoint returns HTTP 503 with status 'down' and api.available false, without showing error details.\",\n    \"A successful probe that takes 1000 ms or more returns HTTP 200 with status 'degraded'.\",\n    \"environment follows C-ENV, and version equals the version in package.json. commit is a 7-character SHA on Vercel and null locally.\",\n    \"The response and the page contain no Supabase URL, no key and no environment variable names or values beyond the agreed fields.\",\n    \"/status renders the environment, version, commit when present, check time and a state label for 'ok', 'degraded', 'down' and mock mode, with an indicator that does not rely on color alone and a working refresh button.\",\n    \"The /status page gets its data from lib/status.ts on the server and does not fetch /api/status over HTTP.\",\n    \"Anonymous users are not redirected away from /status or /api/status, and the existing protected routes keep their redirects.\",\n    \"Build output shows /status and /api/status as dynamic, not prerendered.\",\n    \"The new test files pass, and the existing tests carrito, mock, data-fallback and tipos pass unchanged.\",\n    \"One full npm run verify passes with no check skipped or failed, including docs, tooling, test, lint, typecheck and build.\",\n    \"README.md and PROJECT_GUIDE.md describe the page and the endpoint, and npm run docs:check passes.\",\n    \"There are no new dependencies, no new environment variables, no changes to the nested resuelvelo/ tree and no changes to proxy.ts, lib/supabase/proxy.ts or vitest.config.ts.\",\n    \"The browser pass of /status in mock mode is done. Preview and Production checks are recorded as pending until a deploy is authorized.\"\n  ],\n  \"risks\": [\n    \"If the route or page is statically prerendered, environment, version and commit freeze at build time. Next 16 conventions differ from what the workers may expect, so they must check node_modules/next/dist/docs and confirm the result in build output.\",\n    \"This is the repository's first Route Handler. The global jsdom test environment may not support Request and Response properly, so route tests may need a per-file node environment pragma.\",\n    \"Modules read environment variables when they load (for example SUPABASE_DISPONIBLE). Tests that skip resetModules and dynamic imports can leak stubbed values into each other.\",\n    \"A live probe on every request adds latency and load, on top of the auth.getUser() call proxy.ts already makes. Heavy polling of a public endpoint could add Supabase traffic; there is no rate limit or caching in this plan.\",\n    \"The Supabase health endpoint shows whether Supabase is reachable, not whether every database table or RLS policy works, so 'available' is a coarse signal.\",\n    \"Environment and commit on Preview and Production cannot be verified locally and depend on Vercel exposing its system environment variables.\",\n    \"Showing the environment, version and commit publicly reveals a little information about the deployment.\",\n    \"Workers could edit files in the nested resuelvelo/ tree, and lint or typecheck could pick that tree up.\",\n    \"Only one process may use .next/ at a time. If a worker runs typecheck, build or dev while QA runs verify, results become unreliable.\",\n    \"Codex's planning report was empty because it never received the feature text, so the backend tasks were defined by other roles and need codex to acknowledge them before work starts.\"\n  ],\n  \"open_questions\": [\n    \"What should 'API availability' mean? Proposed: a Supabase health probe with a 3000 ms timeout, where a successful probe at 1000 ms or more counts as 'degraded'. The alternative is reporting only that the route itself responds.\",\n    \"How should mock mode be reported? Proposed: status 'ok' with api.mode 'mock' and HTTP 200.\",\n    \"Should the endpoint return HTTP 503 when status is 'down'? Proposed: yes. The alternative is always returning 200 with a status field.\",\n    \"What should 'backend version' be? Proposed: the package.json version plus a nullable short VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA.\",\n    \"Which environment source is authoritative? Proposed: VERCEL_ENV, falling back to NODE_ENV, with no new APP_ENV variable.\",\n    \"Should /status and /api/status be fully public, including environment, version and commit in production? Proposed: yes.\",\n    \"Should the page refresh manually only, using router.refresh(), with no automatic polling? Proposed: yes.\",\n    \"Should a /status link be added to the Footer (task FE-3)? Proposed: yes, a single link.\",\n    \"Should documentation stay in README.md and PROJECT_GUIDE.md only, with no new indexed document? Proposed: yes.\",\n    \"Is the nested resuelvelo/ directory intentional? Proposed: confirm it is out of scope for all workers.\",\n    \"Will a deploy be authorized so the environment and commit can be checked on Preview and Production? Until then that check stays pending.\"\n  ]\n}","session_id":"53c8a7b9-2eea-4626-a51c-bfdb1dc53626","request_id":"965c63a7-bd85-48d2-b878-b40e349c7c5b","usage":{"inputTokens":8,"outputTokens":12279,"cacheReadTokens":103592,"cacheWriteTokens":14113}}
